# Skills

## Consumer skills (shipped)

Each skill is a folder in `packages/permdock/skills/`, written for the consumer's repo:

- `permdock`: the entry skill. Mental model, consumer invariants, `explain`, CLI checks, the docs MCP, and which skill to load for which task.
- `permdock-wire`: first setup (define, policy basics, factory file, first guard, CLI checks). `references/adapters.md` holds the HTTP, UI, provider and database factory shapes.
- `permdock-audit`: review an app or a pull request (inventory, ungranted and unused leaves, validation, ASI02 / ASI03, PR review), then the Verify list of each topic skill in use.
- `permdock-agents`: tool maps per runtime, subject and actor, `delegation` and `delegations`, A2A, WebMCP, Web Bot Auth. `references/runtimes.md` holds the agent adapter shapes.
- `permdock-approvals`: `approval` grants, approvers, quorum, escalation, stores and the resume flow.
- `permdock-tenancy`: named scopes, memberships, ownership rules and custom roles.
- `permdock-data`: `filter()` / `where()`, ORM adapters, generated RLS, the relationship graph and parity tests.
- `permdock-credentials`: JWT and introspection subjects, API keys and service accounts, share links.

Rules for these skills:

- Names are `permdock` or `permdock-<topic>`, never unprefixed, because installed skills from every publisher share one flat folder ([decision 0017](../../docs/decisions/0017-permdock-skill-prefix.md)).
- `SKILL.md` stays short: Inputs, Invariants, a numbered Workflow whose steps end in a "✓" check, Verify before done, and a Reference index. Long material goes in `references/*.md`, linked from the step that needs it.
- A skill names another skill and its install command (`npx skills add ScaleDockHQ/PermDock --skill <name>`), never a relative link across skill folders. Protocol rules defer to the neutral spec skill (`npx skills add ScaleDockHQ/scaledock-skills --skill <name>`) instead of restating the spec.
- PermDock only: no stack defaults, and an adapter is named only where PermDock ships it. Every identifier, option, flag, doctor code and denial reason is checked against `packages/permdock/src` and the docs, and each concept links its permdock.dev page.
- A topic-specific review item lives in that topic skill's Verify list, not in `permdock-audit`.
- Consumer instructions never go in `AGENTS.md` or `.agents/rules`, and maintainer instructions never go in these skills.
- Frontmatter follows the [Agent Skills spec](https://agentskills.io/specification): `name` (matches the folder), `description` (starts with what it does, because pickers show about 57 characters, then when to use it; third person; at most 1024 characters), `license: MIT`, and `metadata` with `author`, `homepage` and `repository` as strings. No version in `metadata`: skills version with the `permdock` package.
- They reach users three ways, all from the same folders: `npx skills add ScaleDockHQ/PermDock`, `permdock skills` from `node_modules/permdock/skills`, and the Claude Code plugin in `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` (`/plugin marketplace add ScaleDockHQ/permdock`). Adding a skill updates `SKILL_NAMES` in `packages/permdock/src/cli/skills.ts`, the marketplace `skills` array, `cli/skills.mdx` and `for-ai-agents.mdx`.
- `npx skills add ScaleDockHQ/PermDock --list` must list only `permdock`, `permdock-wire`, `permdock-audit`, `permdock-agents`, `permdock-approvals`, `permdock-tenancy`, `permdock-data` and `permdock-credentials`. Run it after touching skill folders or the marketplace file.

## Vendored skills (maintainer tooling)

- `.agents/skills/` holds third-party skills for agents working in this repo, pinned by source and hash in `skills-lock.json`. `.cursor/skills` and `.claude/skills` symlink into it.
- Refresh or add one with `npx skills add <source> --skill <name>`, which updates the lock. Never edit a vendored skill in place; the next update overwrites it.
- They are hidden from ripgrep (`.ignore`) and from Cursor indexing (`.cursorignore`) because each match would appear three times; skills load by path.
- If `skills add … --list` ever shows a vendored skill to consumers, stop committing `.agents/skills`: gitignore it and restore it from `skills-lock.json` on install.
